      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO GRAVITATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Universal Law of Gravitation details the mutual attraction between two masses in the universe.",
        "Acceleration due to gravity (g) is subject to variations based on location, depth, and altitude.",
        "Mass represents the quantity of matter in an object, while Weight measures the gravitational force acting upon it.",
        "Thrust, pressure, buoyancy, and Archimedes' principle govern the behavior of objects immersed in fluids."
      ],
      "id": "naf8bou"
